+### The Simple / Detailed switch, 29 Oct 2026 (branch `feat/demo-polish`)
+
+A two-button switch ("How much to show") on `/analysis` and `/advisory` that hides the working and keeps the verdict. It was row 8 of the owner's feature table. It changes no backend code, so the suite is still 2,189 tests; the dictionaries are 898 keys (7,184 values) after its 4 `detail.*` keys.
+
+- **The default was Detailed when this was built; the owner changed it to Simple later the same day (see the last bullet).** The row did not say which side. Simple hides, on `/analysis`, the money and business cards, the local market, "Show the full working", what we noticed and the government-support list; on `/advisory`, the four advice cards, the loan options, the scheme-funding card, the registrations card and the details disclosure. A judge who never finds the switch would miss exactly the work built during the hackathon, so a choice nobody made reads as Detailed (`DEFAULT_DETAIL` in `DetailSwitch.jsx`). To flip it, change that constant and make every browser verifier that seeds `localStorage` seed `'detailed'` (about eleven, each seeds on its own); otherwise they measure Simple pages and fail.
+- **Design.** The choice is a display preference like the language and the theme: `localStorage['sih-detail']`, never the financial answers, and it is written by a press and never on mount. `DetailSwitch` sets `<html data-detail>` in a layout effect (so Simple never flashes the sections it hides) and deletes it on unmount, so `/report`, which has no switch, always prints everything. A page marks its detail with `.ui-detail-only` and `index.css` hides that class under `[data-detail="simple"]`; the switch knows no section. `display: none` removes a hidden section from the accessibility tree too. `useState(readDetail)` reads the key again on every mount, which is how a choice made on `/analysis` is there on `/advisory`. Simple keeps the light, the verdict, the next steps and (with the helper on) the written-plan card; it adds a one-line note saying how to see the rest.
+- **Written test first.** The `drive` check (see `tools/README.md`, "Simple or Detailed") exited 1 with 17 findings against the page without the switch: 13 failing looks and the 4 presses with no button to press. After the component it exits 0 with 13 looks and 48 loads.
+- **Trap: a uniqueness proof that proved nothing.** The first green attempt exited 2. The check wants each name to be printed exactly once with everything shown, and it counted substrings of `document.body.innerText`, where the summary sentence "Your business is in a good position." holds the heading "Your business". It now reads `#main`, matches whole lines (or the line after the icon that leads one), and throws, listing every offender, which is exit 2.
+- **Trap: a profile that outlives the run.** `drive`'s Edge profile persists, so a leftover `sih-detail` would make the next run's passes load Simple. Each pass's seed sets the key (to `'detailed'` since the default became Simple) and the check ends with it removed.
+- **Two real findings on the first full gate run (21 of 23 green), neither of which `drive` could see.** `mobile-audit` exited 1: Malayalam at 320 px and the largest text, `320-stress_advisory`, `CLIP` twice, the row 307 px wide in a 296 px box. A flex item's automatic minimum width is its min-content, here two full words plus padding, and nothing let the segments shrink. The switch now has `max-width: 100%`, its segments have `flex: 1 1 auto` and `overflow-wrap: anywhere`, and the words wrap inside them only as a last resort (at a 22 px root font they do, and the switch holds the 296 px ceiling). `lang-layout` exited 1: `FLUSH` once on `/analysis` in all 8 languages at 1440 and 1280, because the two segments share an edge, as they should. The `A-`/`A`/`A+` trio was already exempt for that reason, so `.ui-detail-switch` joined it. A one-off probe outside the repo (8 languages × 3 text sizes × 320 and 360 px × both modes × both pages, 192 loads) read 4 clipped rows before the fix, all Malayalam at 320 px and the largest size, and 0 after; widths below 320 px measure the page, not the switch, because the app's document is never narrower.
+- **How it was checked.** Seven defects were planted in three runs, each caught by the finding meant for it, and the files put back with `cp` and a `sha256` check (the list is in `tools/README.md`). `print-audit` was refuted by taking the switch out of the print rule: exit 1, `[CHROME] .ui-detail is still laid out under media:print`.
+- **Gates run on the finished tree (29 Oct 2026, exit 0 for all 23, plus `drive`).** `parity4` 9 checks; `keycheck` 0 leaked, 0 untranslated, 0 unmapped; `glyph-audit` the 3 documented hits; `node --test` 185, 45, 41 and 74 passed; ESLint clean; `pytest` 2,189 passed in 16.4 s; `mobile-audit` 50 page loads, `print-audit` 6 print renders, `lang-layout` 112 loads, `text-align`, `field-align` 96 loads, `motion-audit`, `brand-mark` 2 modes, `hero-art` 3 modes, `manual-audit` 3 modes, `error-banner` 32 cases, `scroll-audit` 38 hops, `figure-audit` 352 measurements, `market-ui` 42 loads, each 0 findings; `talk-ui` 460 checks, 0 failed. `drive` on the restored tree: 13 looks at the switch, 48 loads, 0 findings. Not run on this tree: `hero-geom`, `hero-vibrance`, `load-perf` (reports only).
+- **Trap: gates leave Edge behind.** After the first full run 10 headless Edge processes were still alive (profiles `edge-profile-*`), after the `print-audit` refuter runs 1 was, and after the final run 10 again (the ports of `print-audit`, `lang-layout`, `text-align`, `field-align`, `motion-audit`, `brand-mark`, `hero-art`, `manual-audit`, `error-banner` and `scroll-audit`). They were found by `Get-CimInstance Win32_Process` (a `msedge.exe` with `--remote-debugging-port` and no `--type=`) and killed by PID. The owner's own Edge (`--no-startup-window`) is not one of them. This is the "Edge leaks" gap listed under "Verifier exit codes".
