+### Market rows for 18 more districts, 29 Oct 2026 (branch `feat/demo-polish`)
+
+Row 6 of the owner's feature table. The owner named 15 lines of districts; they are 18 districts in 8 states: Ranchi and East Singhbhum (Jharkhand), Begusarai and Muzaffarpur (Bihar), Guna (Madhya Pradesh), North 24 Parganas, South 24 Parganas, Murshidabad, Purba Bardhaman and Paschim Bardhaman (West Bengal), Prayagraj, Kanpur Nagar, Kanpur Dehat and Pratapgarh (Uttar Pradesh), Rangareddy (Telangana), Ahmedabad (Gujarat), and Dhubri and Kamrup (Assam). The table went from 125 rows for 13 districts in 12 states to 291 rows for 31 districts in 15 states: 217 business counts (7 for every district) and 74 crop prices. No code changed. The two fetch scripts are frozen by `script_sha256`, and every row from 24 Sept to 29 Oct carries the same one (`52634a91…`), so the code that wrote the 24 Sept rows is the code that wrote these.
+
+- **How the lines were read.** "Bardhaman (East/West)" is two districts (Purba and Paschim); so are "Kanpur Nagar/Dehat" and "Dhubri & Kamrup". "Murshibad" was read as Murshidabad. "Kamrup" was taken as Kamrup and not Kamrup Metropolitan, and "Pratapgarh" as the Uttar Pradesh one (the line says so; Rajasthan has a Pratapgarh too). The owner was told in the reply; nobody has confirmed the readings.
+- **The names do not agree, so the crosswalk grew (`tools/market-crosswalk.json`, version 3).** The Ministry spells "NORTH 24 PRAGANAS", "SOUTH 24 PRAGANAS", "RANGA REDDI" and "AHMADABAD", and Ranchi's entry has a trailing space (`"RANCHI "`). Agmarknet files Rangareddy under "Ranga Reddy" and Kerala under "Keralam". The file now has 7 district aliases (Faizabad, Allahabad, Kheri, the two 24 Parganas, Ranga Reddi, Ahmadabad) and 1 State alias (Keralam), so a dropdown spelling reaches the Ministry's. Eight entries have their Agmarknet name set by hand (`origin: manual`): Lucknow and Varanasi (from September) and Ranchi, East Singhbhum, Kanpur Nagar, Kanpur Dehat, Dhubri and Pratapgarh. A test round-trips the shipped file byte for byte, so each entry stays on one line.
+- **The run, in order.** Three crosswalk-proposal runs (22:04, 22:11, 22:16) wrote only `.market-cache/crosswalk-proposal.json` and were used to find the names that did not match (87, then 85, then 83 districts unmatched). The write at 22:17 fetched all 18 and took about 34 minutes, mostly paging the Ministry's Udyam list (Ranchi alone lists 1,22,269 units). Five districts came back with no price (Ranchi, East Singhbhum, South 24 Parganas, Kanpur Nagar, Dhubri). Their Agmarknet names were set in the crosswalk by hand, a dry run at 22:57 checked them, and a write at 23:02 with `--keep-others` fetched those five again. The first run's counts for them were replaced, not added to.
+- **Why five districts have no crop price.** Guntur (fetched on 27 Oct; the 60 days read hold 560 Agmarknet rows, 490 of other crops and 70 of a variety we do not allow, so none is kept). South 24 Parganas (Agmarknet returned no rows; its `agmarknet_district` list is empty). Ranchi, East Singhbhum and Dhubri: the latest report Agmarknet holds is from September 2020, January 2019 and about April 2026, each more than 30 days before the fetch, so none is shown. All five show their 7 business counts. A price from a neighbouring district is never borrowed (the rule in CLAUDE.md, "Market context").
+- **Nine rows are `stale`.** Wheat, paddy and potato for Kanpur Dehat, Kanpur Nagar and Pratapgarh were last reported on 21 Oct, 8 days before the fetch, which is the threshold. The pages print `mk.stale` for them.
+- **Kanpur Nagar rests on a reading.** Agmarknet files the Kanpur city mandis as "Kanpur"; we took that to be Kanpur Nagar. It is our reading, unconfirmed with Agmarknet, and `DATA_SOURCES.md` lists it as UNRESOLVED.
+- **`market_data.provenance.json` describes only the last run.** Its `districts_attempted` lists the five of 23:02, and its `rows_by_metric` (74 prices, 217 counts) is the whole file. The per-row `provenance.fetched_at` is the record that says which run wrote which district: 24 Sept (Lucknow, Varanasi), 27 Oct (11), 29 Oct 22:17 (13), 29 Oct 23:02 (5). Its test checks the shape and not the contents.
+- **The Udyam list changes daily.** Its `updated_date` was 2026-10-29T07:30:47Z. The resume checkpoints in `.market-cache/` are reused only while that date and the unit total are unchanged, so after the next update (about 13:00 IST) a rerun reads the big districts from the start. Start the Row 5 refetch with time to spare: this run, for 18 districts, took about 34 minutes.
