+### The organisers' second reply and the 12:24 PM ET line, 30 Oct 2026 (branch `feat/demo-polish`)
+
+The owner sent the organisers follow-up questions in Discord. The Cerebral Valley app account (an automated account again) replied the same day, and the reply is transcribed in `docs/HACKATHON.md` §9.1. It ends by saying the organisers have been asked about "the rest" and will answer in the thread, so a human answer on the layout of the submission repository is still to come.
+
+- **What it says.** Building started when the kickoff ended, at 12:24 PM ET on 26 Oct. Anything written before then counts as pre-existing work, the work from 12:00 to 12:24 PM included. The submitted repository must be public, created on 26 Oct or later, and hold only work done during the event, with the pre-existing code and its git history kept out; the README must name the pre-existing work; the video opens with one line saying what existed before and what was built this week; and **the event code must also run on its own from the repo's setup instructions.**
